Price and admit Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 for ARTISAN's text roles; send it requests it accepts.

Rates read 2026-11-13 at https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing:
$4 input, $0.20 cache reads, $5 5-minute and $8 1-hour cache writes, $20 output
per 1M tokens. Its output_config.effort accepts low, medium, high, xhigh and max.

- pipeline/cost.py: the claude-opus-5-5 price row.
- pipeline/providers.py: xhigh and max are admitted for anthropic claude-opus-5-5;
  the OpenAI check after it is unchanged.
- pipeline/llm/anthropic.py:
  - every Messages request is streamed and read with get_final_message();
  - stop_reason "refusal" raises AnthropicRefusalError, and "max_tokens" inside a
    tool call raises AnthropicIncompleteToolCallError; neither is retried;
  - claude-opus-5-5 is sent thinking {"type": "adaptive"} with
    block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior "drop_block" under the
    thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01 beta, because the harness edits earlier
    turns at session boundaries (pipeline/context_policy.py) and this model binds
    its thinking blocks to the conversation that produced them.
  No sampling parameter, prefill or forced tool choice is sent (none was before),
  thinking is never disabled, and max_tokens is always set.

Not selected by default: the provider and model come from ARTISAN_PIPELINE_PROVIDER
and ARTISAN_PIPELINE_MODEL. Nothing in the OpenAI path changes.

Applied after 0002-gpt-6-1-sol.patch, against
physicalvision/Artisan@ad322b5b31e50bdb84155520f09622c00c6056c3.

